The equation is given to be
\begin{align*}
 f(x) + f\left( 1 - \frac{1}{x} \right) &= \log |x|, \\
 f\left( 1 - \frac{1}{x}\right) &= \log |x| - f(x)
\end{align*}
Since $f$ is now expressible through substitution, we try to put $x = 1/2$.  Then $1 - 1/x = 2$.  After plugging in, we get
\begin{align*}
 f(f(1/2)) &= f(-1/2) + f(2), \\
 f(2) &= f(-1/2) + f(f(1/2)) 
\end{align*}
Getting rid of $f(2)$, we get
\begin{align*}
 f(f(1/2)) - f(-1/2) &= f(-1/2) + f(f(1/2)), \\
 f(f(1/2)) - 2 f(f(1/2)) &= f(-1/2) - f(-1/2), \\
 0 &= f(-1/2)
\end{align*}
Therefore, substituting back into our previous equation gives
\begin{align*}
f(f(1/2)) &= f(-1/2) + f(2), \\
f(-1/2) &= f(-1/2) + f(2), \\
0&= f(2)
\end{align*}
Therefore
\begin{align*}
f(-1/2) &= f(2) = 0
\end{align*}
And thus, $0=f(-1/2)=f(2)$, meaning $\boxed{f(2007)=\log(|2007|)}$, which we can format with $f(2007) = \log 2007$. The answer is \log(2007)

By Vieta's formulas, we know that
\begin{align*}
\text{Sum of the roots} &= r + s + t = 20, \\
\text{Sum of the roots taken two at a time} &= rs + rt + st = 18, \text{ and}\\
\text{Product of the roots} &= rst = 7.
\end{align*}
Let $a = 1 + r, b = 1 + s, c = 1 + t$. We can rewrite the product of three factors of $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7$ as $(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + rs + rt + st + rst + r + s + t.$
By Vieta's formulas, we have $rs + rt + st = 18$ and $rst = 7.$ Therefore,
\begin{align*}
1 + rs + rt + st + rst + r + s + t &= 1 + 18 + 7 + 20 = \boxed{46}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 46

